-- title:
--   Syndrome-based probabilistic cellular automata: local rules, runs and memory
-- statement:
--   Let $C=\ker H$ be a classical linear code on $n$ bits. An update rule $a=(a_1,\dots,a_n)$, $a_i:\operatorname{im}H\to\mathbb F_2$, is **$R$-local** if each $a_i$ depends only on the syndrome bits $s_j$ whose parity check has support within graph distance $R$ of bit $i$ in the interaction graph of $C$.
--
--   A **run at stochastic-adversarial fault rate $p$, started at $e_0$,** is a random sequence $(e_r)_{r\ge0}$ on some probability space with $e_0$ given and
--   $$e_{r+1}=e_r\oplus a(He_r)\oplus\zeta_r,\qquad \operatorname{supp}\zeta_r\subseteq F_r ,$$
--   where each fault set $F_r\subseteq\{1,\dots,n\}$ contains each site independently with probability $p$, independently of $e_0,\dots,e_r$ and $F_0,\dots,F_{r-1}$, and the fault vector $\zeta_r$ is otherwise arbitrary (it may depend on the whole history, on $F_r$ and on extra randomness). The SPCA **started at $e_0$ $q$-remembers $b$ through round $m$** if every such run satisfies $\Pr[b(e_r)\neq b(e_0)]\le q$ for all $r\le m$.
--
--   These are the classical hypotheses of Theorem 4.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Every run" quantifies over every probability space. The fault vector is implicit: the update condition only constrains $e_{r+1}$ outside $F_r$. Independence is factorization of probabilities on atoms, since all variables are finite-valued. Locality is required only between valid syndromes.
-- source:
--   Drechsler, Oreg, Aharonov, Autonomous Quantum Memories from Classical Stochastic Processes, arXiv:2610.05589 (PDF of 2026-11-03), Definition 2.40, eqs. (75)–(76), p. 28 (PDF p. 30); Definition 2.21, p. 19 (PDF p. 21)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AutoQMem_Lindblad_Supplement_interactionGraph
open Matrix

namespace AutoQMem.Lindblad.Supplement

open AutoQMem.Lindblad MeasureTheory

variable {m n : ℕ}

/-- **R-local syndrome-based update rule.** Drechsler, Oreg, Aharonov, *Autonomous Quantum Memories
from Classical Stochastic Processes*, arXiv:2610.05589 (PDF of 2026-11-03), Definition 2.40, item 1,
p. 28 (PDF 30): "a = (a_1, …, a_n) is a vector of Boolean functions a_i : Im H → 𝔽₂ … Each a_i
depends only on syndrome bits s_j whose corresponding parity check has support within graph distance
R of bit i", distances in the interaction graph of `C = ker H`.

**Formalization Note.** `a` is total on `𝔽₂^m`; the locality condition is imposed only between
valid syndromes `s, s' ∈ im H`, matching `a_i : Im H → 𝔽₂`. -/
def IsLocalRule (H : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) (ZMod 2)) (R : ℕ)
    (a : (Fin m → ZMod 2) → (Fin n → ZMod 2)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (i : Fin n) (s s' : Fin m → ZMod 2), s ∈ Set.range H.mulVec → s' ∈ Set.range H.mulVec →
    (∀ j, (∀ k, H j k ≠ 0 → (checkGraph H).edist i k ≤ R) → s j = s' j) → a s i = a s' i

/-- **A run of the SPCA at stochastic-adversarial fault rate p, started at e₀.** Drechsler, Oreg,
Aharonov, *Autonomous Quantum Memories from Classical Stochastic Processes*, arXiv:2610.05589 (PDF of
2026-11-03), Definition 2.40, eqs. (75)–(76), p. 28 (PDF 30): "e_{r+1} = Ψ(e_r) = e_r ⊕ a(He_r) ⊕ ζ_r
… At each round r, a random fault-location set F_r ⊆ {1, …, n} is drawn by including each site
independently with probability p, independently of e_0, …, e_r and of F_0, …, F_{r−1}. The fault
vector ζ_r is otherwise unrestricted: it may be random and may depend on the entire history and on
F_r, subject only to supp(ζ_r) ⊆ F_r. … A run of Ψ is a process (e_r)_{r≥0} generated by this map
for some choice of fault vectors ζ_r satisfying the conditions above."

**Formalization Note.**
* The run lives on an arbitrary probability space `(Ω, P)`; `e r ω` is `e_r`, `F r ω` is `F_r`.
  The fault vector is `ζ_r = e_{r+1} − e_r − a(He_r)`, so "`e_{r+1} = e_r + a(He_r) + ζ_r` with
  `supp ζ_r ⊆ F_r`" is `update`; nothing else constrains `ζ_r`.
* "Each site independently with probability p" is the product law of `F_r`; independence of `F_r`
  from `(e_0, …, e_r, F_0, …, F_{r−1})` is written as factorization on atoms (all variables are
  finite-valued). The events are required to be measurable. -/
structure IsSPCARun (H : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) (ZMod 2)) (a : (Fin m → ZMod 2) → (Fin n → ZMod 2))
    (p : ℝ) (e0 : Fin n → ZMod 2) {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
    (e : ℕ → Ω → Fin n → ZMod 2) (F : ℕ → Ω → Finset (Fin n)) : Prop where
  /-- The configurations are random variables. -/
  meas_e : ∀ r v, MeasurableSet {ω | e r ω = v}
  /-- The fault sets are random variables. -/
  meas_F : ∀ r S, MeasurableSet {ω | F r ω = S}
  /-- Started at `e₀`. -/
  init : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, e 0 ω = e0
  /-- `e_{r+1} = e_r ⊕ a(H e_r) ⊕ ζ_r` with `supp ζ_r ⊆ F_r` (eqs. (75)–(76)). -/
  update : ∀ r, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ i, i ∉ F r ω → e (r + 1) ω i = e r ω i + a (H *ᵥ e r ω) i
  /-- `F_r` includes each site independently with probability `p`. -/
  bernoulli : ∀ r S, (P {ω | F r ω = S}).toReal = p ^ S.card * (1 - p) ^ (n - S.card)
  /-- `F_r` is independent of `e_0, …, e_r` and `F_0, …, F_{r−1}`. -/
  indep : ∀ r S (v : Fin (r + 1) → Fin n → ZMod 2) (T : Fin r → Finset (Fin n)),
    (P ({ω | F r ω = S} ∩
        {ω | (∀ k : Fin (r + 1), e k.val ω = v k) ∧ ∀ k : Fin r, F k.val ω = T k})).toReal =
      (P {ω | F r ω = S}).toReal *
        (P {ω | (∀ k : Fin (r + 1), e k.val ω = v k) ∧ ∀ k : Fin r, F k.val ω = T k}).toReal

/-- **The SPCA, started at e₀, q-remembers b through round m.** Drechsler, Oreg, Aharonov,
*Autonomous Quantum Memories from Classical Stochastic Processes*, arXiv:2610.05589 (PDF of
2026-11-03), Definition 2.40, p. 28 (PDF 30): "For b : Ω → S, we say that Ψ, started at e_0,
q-remembers b through round m if every run of Ψ with initial configuration e_0 q-remembers b through
round m in the sense of Definition 2.21", i.e. `sup_{0 ≤ r ≤ m} Pr[b(e_r) ≠ b(e_0)] ≤ q`.

**Formalization Note.** "Every run" quantifies over every probability space `Ω : Type` and every
adversary, so the adversary keeps its full freedom (history dependence, extra randomness). -/
def SPCARemembers (H : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) (ZMod 2)) (a : (Fin m → ZMod 2) → (Fin n → ZMod 2))
    (p : ℝ) (e0 : Fin n → ZMod 2) (b : (Fin n → ZMod 2) → ZMod 2) (mr : ℕ) (q : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (Ω : Type) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (e : ℕ → Ω → Fin n → ZMod 2) (F : ℕ → Ω → Finset (Fin n)),
    IsSPCARun H a p e0 P e F → ∀ r : ℕ, r ≤ mr → (P {ω | b (e r ω) ≠ b (e 0 ω)}).toReal ≤ q

end AutoQMem.Lindblad.Supplement


